WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.393
Practical IEC 62443 adoption begins with scope and ownership.

00:00:05.393 --> 00:00:15.409
Define the system under consideration, the physical process it supports, responsible organizations, lifecycle stage, and risk decision makers.

00:00:15.409 --> 00:00:24.911
Build an asset inventory that includes devices, software, firmware, communication paths, remote connections, suppliers, and operational dependencies.

00:00:24.911 --> 00:00:29.277
Perform risk assessment with engineers and operators.

00:00:29.277 --> 00:00:35.697
Identify credible threats, vulnerabilities, existing safeguards, process consequences, and required recovery.

00:00:35.697 --> 00:00:42.631
Use the results to define zones, conduits, target security levels, and requirements.

00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:50.592
Avoid copying an architecture from another site without confirming that functions and consequences match.

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:55.985
Review the architecture for unnecessary connectivity and uncontrolled trust.

00:00:55.985 --> 00:01:02.919
Design segmentation, secure remote access, administration, monitoring, backups, and update pathways together.

00:01:02.919 --> 00:01:11.907
Procurement and supplier requirements should state expected capabilities, evidence, vulnerability handling, support periods, and integration assumptions.

00:01:11.907 --> 00:01:23.464
During implementation, configure component security features, remove unused functions, manage identities and privileges, document exceptions, and test controls under realistic conditions.

00:01:23.464 --> 00:01:29.884
Acceptance testing should verify security behavior as well as process operation.

00:01:29.884 --> 00:01:38.359
The asset owner needs accurate diagrams, account ownership, configuration records, backup procedures, and recovery information.

00:01:38.359 --> 00:01:47.861
Operation requires change control, vulnerability management, monitoring, incident response, periodic access review, backup testing, and lifecycle planning.

00:01:47.861 --> 00:01:57.877
Evidence should show what was implemented, who approved it, how it was tested, and how deviations are managed.

00:01:57.877 --> 00:02:03.783
Metrics should support decisions rather than exist only for reporting.

00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:09.690
Organizations do not need to solve every issue at once.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:21.247
Start with high-consequence systems and pathways, create achievable improvement plans, and integrate cybersecurity with existing engineering, safety, reliability, and maintenance processes.

00:02:21.247 --> 00:02:28.694
IEC 62443 works best as an operating discipline, not a one-time documentation project.
